        <body>
            <div xml:id="d460">

                <pb facs="0692" n="592" sameAs="frus:frus1884/pg592"/>

                <head>No. 460.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Baker to Mr. Frelinghuysen.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1884-06-01"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 1, 1884</date>.
                        (Received June 10.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 941.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my No. 918, of date 6th
                    ultimo, relative to the case of Mr. John E. Wheelock, I have the honor to
                    inclose herewith a copy of a note, of date 31st ultimo, which I addressed to
                    Senor Amengual, <pb facs="0693" n="593" xml:id="pg593"/> relative to the same
                    matter, and also relative to the general position of this Government in regard
                    to remanding to the high federal court claims presented by the Government of the
                    United States against the Government of Venezuela;. The latter part was written
                    in view of what you say relative to the matter in your dispatch numbered 286, of
                    date 8th of April last, taken in connection with your note to Mr. Soteldo, of
                    date 4th of April last, a copy of which was sent as an inclosure with your said
                    dispatch, and also in connection with your dispatch numbered 296, of date 8th
                    ultimo. * * *</p>
                <p>I believe you will find the substance of the matter condensed and clearly
                    expressed in the concluding part of my note to Señor Amengual.</p>
                <p>As this matter is of very high legal and practical importance, I draw your
                    special attention to this note.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JEHU BAKER.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d460-a1.xml" xpointer="d460-a1"/>
            </div>
